%9Setting:%9

    sidepanel_debug (boolean; default: OFF)

%9Description:%9

    Writes a debug log of the side panels and the mouse: clicks, scrolls,
    gestures, window switches and how the panels are laid out. For
    tracking down a problem with the panels or the mouse; leave it off
    otherwise.

    The log is sidepanels.log in the erssi home (~/.erssi/sidepanels.log
    unless erssi was started with --home), readable only by you: it holds
    the names of your windows and channels and nicks. A link or anything
    but a file of your own in its place is not written to. ON opens the
    log at once and appends to it, OFF closes it.

%9Examples:%9

    /SET sidepanel_debug on
    /EXEC -interactive tail -f ~/.erssi/sidepanels.log
    /SET sidepanel_debug off

%9See also:%9

    SET, RESIZE_DEBUG

